Fig. 9.1 shows the visible part of the emission spectrum from hydrogen gas in a laboratory on the Earth. The numbers indicate the wavelength, in $\text{nm}$, represented by each line.

{{figure:figure_9_1}}

Fig. 9.1

Fig. 9.2 shows five of the energy levels in the hydrogen atom. The wavelengths of radiation shown in Fig. 9.1 relate to transitions to the $-3.400\text{ eV}$ level in Fig. 9.2.

{{figure:figure_9_2}}

Fig. 9.2 (not to scale)
